{"id":"sf-licensing-against-state","title":"San Francisco child-care centres against the other large counties","question":"Are San Francisco centres cited, complained about and visited more or less often than centres elsewhere in California?","finding":"San Francisco's 400 open centres carry 20.8 Type A citations per 100 centres against 42.5 statewide (rank 20 of 26 counties with 100 or more open centres, most cited first). 24% of complaint allegations against them were upheld, against 32% statewide (rank 25 of 26). 78% were visited in the last twelve months (77% statewide); 0 show no visit in three years.","how":"All open (LICENSED) centre licences in the State file of 15 November 2026, grouped by the file's county. Citations add the inspection, other-visit and complaint Type A columns. The upheld share is substantiated allegations over substantiated, inconclusive and unsubstantiated allegations in the file's complaint records. \"Visited\" uses the file's last-visit date against 15 November 2026.","limits":"Counties differ in how many centres are new (fewer visits on record), in centre size and in how often parents complain. A higher citation rate can mean closer inspection rather than worse care. The comparison says nothing about any one centre.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"county","t":"County","type":"text"},{"k":"centres","t":"Open centres","type":"int"},{"k":"places","t":"Places","type":"int"},{"k":"typeAPer100","t":"Type A citations per 100 centres","type":"int"},{"k":"withTypeA","t":"Centres with a Type A citation","type":"pct"},{"k":"complaintsPer100","t":"Complaints per 100 centres","type":"int"},{"k":"upheldShare","t":"Allegations upheld","type":"pct"},{"k":"visitedYear","t":"Visited in last 12 months","type":"pct"},{"k":"noVisit3y","t":"No visit in 3 years","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"county":"Sacramento","centres":603,"places":32618,"typeAPer100":90.9,"withTypeA":0.383,"complaintsPer100":117.4,"upheldShare":0.291,"visitedYear":0.781,"noVisit3y":1},{"c